<title>ITALY: CIR denies looking at French investments.</title>
<headline>CIR denies looking at French investments.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian holding company CIR, controlled by Carlo De Benedetti, denied on Wednesday it was looking at investing in France through its French holding Cerus arm as reported in the weekly magazine Panorama.</p>
<p>The magazine said De Benedetti was planning to take a minority stake in France's Cie des Signaux as well as forming a partnership with &quot;the mobile telephony company of Bordeaux,&quot; and added that he would use his French holding Cerus to carry out the operations.</p>
<p>A statement from CIR described the article as &quot;pure fantasy.&quot; The magazine Panorama is published on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsrrom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
